{%- doc -%}
  The storefront's one free-shipping sentence ("Free shipping over <amount>").

  Every place the theme mentions the free-shipping threshold renders it from
  here, so they can never disagree with each other or with the cart progress
  bar: the cart trust row, the product page's shipping note and truck badge,
  the featured-product badges, the hero trust line and the announcement bar's
  "Free shipping" message. Before this, four of those carried the amount as
  typed text, so the demo quoted one amount in the cart and another on every
  product page.

  Gate and formatting are the cart trust row's: shown only when the progress
  bar is on and a threshold is set (Theme settings > Cart), the amount entered
  in store currency and printed through money_without_trailing_zeros. It is
  formatted BEFORE it is interpolated, so the money filter applies to the value
  and not to the translated sentence. Renders nothing when there is no
  threshold, so callers can capture it and test the result for blank.

  @param {string} [key] - Translation key taking an `amount` argument. Defaults to 'cart.trust.free_shipping_html'.

  @example
  {%- capture claim -%}{% render 'free-shipping-claim' %}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- if claim != blank -%}<span>{{ claim }}</span>{%- endif -%}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- if settings.cart_show_free_shipping_bar and settings.cart_free_shipping_threshold > 0 -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign threshold_money = settings.cart_free_shipping_threshold | times: 100 | money_without_trailing_zeros
    assign claim_key = key | default: 'cart.trust.free_shipping_html'
  -%}
  {{- claim_key | t: amount: threshold_money -}}
{%- endif -%}
